{"type":"standard","title":"Gabe Vasquez","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Gabe Vasquez</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q115155647","titles":{"canonical":"Gabe_Vasquez","normalized":"Gabe Vasquez","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Gabe Vasquez</span></span>"},"pageid":68734135,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Rep_Gabriel_Vasquez_Official_Portrait.jpg/330px-Rep_Gabriel_Vasquez_Official_Portrait.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":413},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/03/Rep_Gabriel_Vasquez_Official_Portrait.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":3360,"height":4200},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1373034814","tid":"c15cc281-a7bb-11f1-bcc6-fbc0d2073046","timestamp":"2026-09-03T17:20:27Z","description":"American politician (born 1984)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gabe_Vasquez","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gabe_Vasquez?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gabe_Vasquez?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Gabe_Vasquez"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gabe_Vasquez","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Gabe_Vasquez","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gabe_Vasquez?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Gabe_Vasquez"}},"extract":"Gabriel Vasquez is an American politician serving as the U.S. representative for New Mexico's 2nd congressional district since 2023. A member of the Democratic Party, he previously served on the Las Cruces City Council from 2017 to 2021. Vasquez's district covers southern New Mexico, including Las Cruces, Carlsbad, and the southern fourth of Albuquerque.","extract_html":"<p><b>Gabriel Vasquez</b> is an American politician serving as the U.S. representative for New Mexico's 2nd congressional district since 2023. A member of the Democratic Party, he previously served on the Las Cruces City Council from 2017 to 2021. Vasquez's district covers southern New Mexico, including Las Cruces, Carlsbad, and the southern fourth of Albuquerque.</p>"}